[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2450668154","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98439#issuecomment-2450668154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98439","id":2450668154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SEjp6","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-31T19:31:20Z","updated_at":"2024-10-31T19:31:20Z","body":"I'm not entirely certain of the original intent behind the `wchar_t`/`char32_t` strings (maybe @dsnopek can clarify), this was more about granting parity. If they're truly redundant, then I suppose they can be discarded. I *guess* `char8_t` could have a niche if `char` was reworked to be specific to ASCII, but that'd involve quite the refactor","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2450668154/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2450690539","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98439#issuecomment-2450690539","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98439","id":2450690539,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SEpHr","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-31T19:45:34Z","updated_at":"2024-10-31T19:45:34Z","body":"> I guess char8_t could have a niche if char was reworked to be specific to ASCII, but that'd involve quite the refactor\r\n\r\nWhy do we want two different type that are exactly same, unless `char8_t` version have some UTF-8 specific methods. Why would it, it's just a wrapper to avoid manual memory management?\r\n\r\n> I'm not entirely certain of the original intent behind the wchar_t/char32_t strings (maybe @dsnopek can clarify), this was more about granting parity.\r\n\r\nNot sure why these exist in the `godot-cpp` either, I guess it was added since there are `string_new_with_wide_chars`, `string_new_with_utf32_chars`, `string_to_utf32_chars`, and `string_to_wide_chars` low level `String` methods (which were intended for use with buffers provided by external API).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2450690539/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2452098679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98439#issuecomment-2452098679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98439","id":2452098679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SKA53","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-01T15:44:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-01T15:44:27Z","body":"> Why do we want two different type that are exactly same\r\n\r\nI *would* say for similar reasons that we use `char16_t`/`char32_t` instead of `uint16_t`/`uint32_t` respectively, but we already have `char` so that's a harder sell. I suppose `char8_t` is explicitly unsigned, making it distinct from both `char` having implementation-defined signedness & `unsigned char` which is just `uint8_t`. Still, probably not the biggest selling point, so it's likely that anything integrating the type would be either part of a wider String refactor or *extremely* barebones","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2452098679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2452140845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98439#issuecomment-2452140845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98439","id":2452140845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SKLMt","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-01T16:10:00Z","updated_at":"2024-11-01T16:14:26Z","body":"> I'm not entirely certain of the original intent behind the wchar_t/char32_t strings (maybe @dsnopek can clarify), this was more about granting parity.\r\n\r\nI also don't really know the intention of `CharWideString` and `Char32String` either. They were added to godot-cpp in PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/602 (which is the original GDNative -> GDExtension PR). Then I just kept them when I did the conversion to a template in PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/1150.\r\n\r\n> Not sure why these exist in the `godot-cpp` either, I guess it was added since there are `string_new_with_wide_chars`, `string_new_with_utf32_chars`, `string_to_utf32_chars`, and `string_to_wide_chars` low level `String` methods (which were intended for use with buffers provided by external API).\r\n\r\nCould be.\r\n\r\nThey end up creating an API discrepancy between Godot and godot-cpp, which isn't great. We probably should consider either (1) removing them from godot-cpp, or (2) adding them to Godot, so the APIs align. If we really do want to have them in godot-cpp for use with external APIs, they wouldn't cause any harm being in Godot as well. Adding them to Godot would probably mean also adding `String::utf32()` and `String::wide_string()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2452140845/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833468635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98439#issuecomment-2833468635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98439","id":2833468635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o40zb","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T13:48:05Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T13:48:05Z","body":"Rebased and refactored! Now the template logic is entirely in the header, reducing code complexity/redundancy even further","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833468635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]